NetHack Trivia Set #003

Amateurs Only
(Please do not answer more than a few [if any] of these questions if
you're an experienced player; they're for newer players to learn [as
well as get involved in trivia]. Though, if you are an experienced
player, please help me write more of these questions, as below; the
interested should e-mail me.)

For ten points each, answer the following NetHack-related questions:
1. Each character class has a different Quest, and thus a different
Quest Nemesis. However, all of them have in their possession an
artifact required to win the game. What is this artifact?

2. The Wizard class is one of the most powerful in the late game, and
the Wizard's Quest Artifact, the Eye of the Aethiopica, is considered
one of the most powerful in the game. It is the sole item in the game
that confers mana regeneration, and also provides magic resistance to
its owner. Who guards this artifact?

3. The Tourist class is a humourous one to play. Some people may find
that this conflicts with the fantasy environment of the dungeon, and
choose not to define tourists when compiling their version of NetHack.
While being a low-level tourist will cause shopkeepers to raise their
prices, openly wearing this piece of "armour" will also have this
effect.

4. Characters playing as Knights always start out as lawful. Starting
Knights are extremely well-equipped, having generous amounts of armour,
food, and charisma, as well as good weapons and a steed. The Knight's
Quest Artifact, the Magic Mirror of Merlin, allows the owner (if he/she
is a Knight) to deal twice as much damage with directed-beam spells.
Who is the leader of the Knight's quest?

5. While the Wizard of Yendor is the player's arch-nemesis, he does not
possess the Amulet of Yendor that is required to win the game. The
Wizard, colloquially known as "Rodney", being "Yendor" spelled
backwards, does have a variety of powers above ordinary spellcasting
abilities, such as the unique ability to produce a clone of himself.
What magical artifact does the Wizard of Yendor have in his possession?

6. This major demon stands guard in a deserted town in the depths of
Gehennom, or Hell. He has a poisoned sting as well as a wand of death,
and like most major demons, he is able to summon other demons and demon
princes to his aid. Who is he?

7. At the entrance to the Valley of the Dead stands a castle defended
by two barracks full of soldiers. In the back rooms of this citadel lie
four stashes of valuable equipment, guarded by a quartet of dragons.
Some players quit once they reach the castle, due to this game-breaking
item that is located in one of the castle's towers. What is it?

8. Taking a drink at one of the fountains found in the Dungeons of Doom
may summon a water demon that will grant you a wish, but more likely
you will experience more negative effects, such as the cursing of items
in your inventory, or the unleashing of hostile monsters. In addition
to the water demon, there is another type of monster that is uniquely
created by disturbing a fountain. What are these creatures that rank
among the top ten causes of death on nethack.alt.org's public NetHack
sever?

9. Although insects rank among the weaker of creatures that one might
find in the depths of the dungeon, they often pose a major threat to
weak players due to their speed, aggressiveness, and poisoned attacks.
One member of the 'a' class is feared more than the rest; what is this
type of insect that is the foremost cause of death on the
nethack.alt.org server?

10. Engraving the word 'Elbereth' on the floor of the dungeon will
cause many types of monsters to flee from you, but only if you are
standing on such a marked square. Placing an item on an 'Elbereth'
square will also cause some hostile monsters to avoid stepping on it.
There is a type of item that, when placed on the ground beneath you,
will scare some creatures; what is it?

11. While you can use a variety of means to write on the dungeon floor,
ranging from scribbling in the dust to carving it in with a hard gem,
only burning it in with a wand of fire or lightning, or vandalising
with a magic marker, will create a permanent message. Carving with
edged weapons will produce a longer-lasting engraving than mere
markings with your fingers; however, this will usually dullen your
blade. One weapon, when not cursed, will not dull by engraving; what is
it?

12. Lewis Carroll was a British writer of many unconventional works, as
well as the authour of various puzzles. He is also known for his fancy
of naked children, but you don't need to know that. The Jabberwocky is
a creature in his poem of the same name, the source of several nonsense
words that are often used in language today, such as 'chortled'. The
Jabberwocky was slain using a sword which also appears in NetHack; what
is the name of this deadly weapon?

13. The number thirteen is often considered as unlucky. Many tall
buildings skip the number thirteen when numbering their floors, or
devote that floor to maintenance equipment. In NetHack, certain dates
and times will affect your luck. The full moon will give you a luck
bonus; a new moon will make you more vulerable to the fatal attack of
this creature. What is this feared monster?

14. Fire is often a deadly weapon in NetHack, though it is rendered
less so when the fire resistance intrinsic is aquired. When you are hit
by a fire attack, potions in your inventory may boil, and scrolls there
may burn, inflicting additional damage upon you. Iron golems will be
healed when a fire-based attack is inflicted upon them, and many demons
are intrinsically fire-resistant. However, monsters with fire
resistance also take double damage when a cold attack is dealt upon
them; what is NetHack's artifact longsword that has a cold-based
attack?

15. The blue dragon has the ability to breathe lightning. Eating the
corpse of one may give you shock resistance, and wearing the scales of
a blue dragon will give it to you extrinsically. Lightning, when
hitting you, may cause rings and wands to explode, dealing considerable
amounts of damage. The wand of lightning is often used to burn
permenant messages into the ground, but will blind you in the process.
Lightning may be hurled at you by an angry god; what is another, more
devastating form of divine attack that you may suffer?

16. In many stories, the wizard Merlin wears a pointy hat. In a Disney
animation, Mickey Mouse appears as a wizard wearing this form of hat,
refered to in NetHack as a cornuthaum. While most wearers of a
cornuthaum will suffer malignant effects, a wizard will be benefited by
wearing one and can safely give it a +7 enchantment. What is this other
form of 'conical hat' that, while usually considered harmful, may
provide valueable defense against mind flayers?

17. The Drow is a dark-elf in Dungeons and Dragons lore, which forms
the basis of much of NetHack. They are known to fight against
illithids, or mind flayers, in the Underdark, and are a playable race
in Slash'EM, the most popular variant of basic, 'vanilla' NetHack.
Elves that you may encounter in vanilla NetHack are resistant to sleep;
what is a type of armour that may give you this ability?

Ok, I'm too tired to write any more of these... moving on.
(3 slime molds to the person who can name this longest-running game
show whose form of questions I based the above trivia upon.)

